# Note components

Spec: `docs/design/design-system.md` §5 and §6.

The notes are the product. A note answers a question of quantity — how many
tokens, how many requests, how many facts survive. Every component in a note
body exists to make one of those countable.

## The figure anatomy

Every figure follows the same seven parts, in this order:

1. **A question as the title.** Not a label — a question the figure answers.
2. **Controls**, only if the reader has something to compare.
3. **The stat**: the number, big, in mono, with its delta chip.
4. **A one-line lede** under the stat.
5. **The plot**.
6. **The legend**.
7. **The caption**, carrying the source and the epistemic basis.

The number is the hero; the plot is the evidence. The stat comes first.

## Use the kit, never hand-roll

`Figure`, `Stat`, `Plot`, `Axis`, `Legend`, `Swatch`, `Toggle`, `Source`,
`DataTable`. If you find yourself writing SVG axis lines, a coordinate system,
a 10×10 swatch or a panel-toggle by hand, you are rebuilding a primitive that
already exists. Use it or extend it.

Number formatting lives in the shared format module. Add to it; do not
reimplement `fmtTokens` or a local rounding helper.

## Every figure declares how it knows

`basis` is required: `measured`, `calculated` or `assumed`. When a figure mixes
sources, the weakest one wins. This is the pedagogical contract of the notes —
the reader must be able to tell a measurement from an assumption.

## Accessibility is not optional

- Every SVG carries `role="img"` and an `aria-label` that states the quantities,
  not the shape.
- Every figure ships a `DataTable` equivalent, hidden visually.
- Toggles are real `<button>` elements with `aria-pressed`, operable by keyboard.
- Tabs need `role="tab"`, `aria-selected` and `aria-controls`.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Animation that teaches must have a still
  end state that teaches the same thing.

## Responsive

SVG scales through `viewBox` plus `width: 100%`. **Never set a pixel
`min-width` on a figure** — that is what forced horizontal scroll on the first
figure of the series. At 390px nothing may overflow horizontally.

## Callouts

Three variants only: `note`, `rule`, `warning`. Sentence case. No emoji, no
ALL-CAPS labels. Red and green mean wrong and right — if your pair is not a
verdict, use neutral and `--data-new` instead.

## Writing

Sentence case everywhere. No tracked-out caps eyebrows. No trailing `→` glued to
static link text. Active voice; say what a thing does, not how the system is
built.
